  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting displaced and crisis-affected populations in the Far North region of CameroonSupporting displaced and crisis-affected populations in the Far North region of Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian needs in Cameroon remain high. According to the Humanitarian Response Plan (HRP) published in April 2024, approximately 3.4 million people are in need of emergency assistance with three humanitarian fronts (Far North Region, North-West, South-West (NWSW) and East Regions. According to the OCHA flood information note from 19 September 2024, flooding has affected at least 365,060 people across five departments in the Far North region of Cameroon: Logone and Chari, Mayo-Danay, Diamar&#xe9;, Mayo-Tsanaga, and Mayo-Kani.In response, IOM is enhancing its humanitarian efforts in the region to better understand displacement trends and sectoral needs. This includes conducting Multi-Sector Needs Assessments (MSNAs) and mobility tracking to address forced displacements and urgent requirements. These assessments will provide comprehensive data on the humanitarian situation, facilitating evidence-based decision-making and targeted interventions. IOM will focus on strengthening data collection through the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) to provide real-time information on population movements and evolving needs.</narrative>
  </description>
